    "title": "Unhoused Man Found Dead In Tent Near D&L Trail In Lehigh County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jillian Pikora ,\n1 days ago\nThe man found dead along a walking path in Pennsylvania has been identified, authorities announced on Wednesday, June 24.\nChristopher Lee Crouthamel, 57, of Allentown, was pronounced dead at 1:35 p.m. on Tuesday, June 23, at the scene in the 200 block of River Street, according to Lehigh County Coroner Daniel Buglio.\nCrouthamel had been residing in a tent near the D&L Trail , the coroner said.\nThe Lehigh County Coroner's Office had previously confirmed to Daily Voice that investigators were called to the scene after reports of a deceased man found along a walking path on Sand Island West.\nThe cause and manner of death remain under investigation. The cause of death is pending toxicology testing, according to the coroner.\nDetails about Crouthamel's life were not immediately available. His loved ones are invited to share information with Daily Voice by emailing jpikora@dailyvoice.com\n21",
    "summary": "The man found dead along a walking path in Pennsylvania has been identified, authorities announced on Wednesday, June 24. Christopher Lee Crouthamel, 57, of Allentown, was pronounced dead at 1:35 p.m. on Tuesday, June 23, at the scene in the 200 block of River Street, according to Lehigh County Coroner Daniel Buglio. Crouthamel had been residing in a tent near the D&L Trail , the coroner said. The Lehigh County Coroner's Office had previously confirmed to Daily Voice that investigators were called to the scene after reports of a deceased man found along a walking path on Sand Island West.",
